<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<form name="frmWoD20_2" align="client" theme="dark">
	<scrollBox align="client">
		<!-- Theme backdrop, same arrangement as WoD20.1 (SPEC T158, V56, V57). -->
		<image name="themePaper2" align="client" style="stretch" hitTest="false" visible="false"/>
		<!--
			Traits grid (SPEC T45). Numina moved to the Powers tab, so merits/flaws and
			derangements moved up into the space they left. Everything closes on x=1362.

			  BACKGROUNDS 0..384      y 0..679
			  MERITS 389..1132        y   0..337      DERANGEMENTS 1137..1362   y   0..337
			  FLAWS  389..1132        y 342..679      OTHER        1137..1362   y 342..679

			47th batch (SPEC I190, user 2026-10-01): that is the MORTAL tab. A vampire's backgrounds
			have NINE dots, so renderGameMode on the root widens BACKGROUNDS by four dots (484) and
			moves the other four boxes 100 right - the tab then closes on 1462 (VAMP_GEOM, SPEC
			V534e, Q109.9). The title and the 21 rows carry anchors="left top right" and stretch
			with the box; dots 6..9 are authored hidden and only a vampire sees them.

			42nd batch (SPEC I186), on the user's ask: BOOK and PAGE doubled (117 -> 234, 45 -> 90)
			and COST grew half (50 -> 75), so a row closes on 703 and MERITS/FLAWS on 743. The nine
			note boxes on the right (ALLIES, MENTOR, RESOURCES, GUIDES, CONTACTS, FAME, ARTIFACTS,
			INFLUENCE, BASE OF OPERATIONS) left; their fields are ORPHANS, so a saved sheet keeps the
			text (SPEC I3, V362b). OTHER grew up to where ARTIFACTS opened (342) and both survivors
			sit 5px right of the tables, the twins of MERITS and FLAWS on the Y axis (SPEC V392b).
			The paragraphs below are the history of the older layouts.
			25th batch (SPEC I170g): BACKGROUNDS grew 20 for the ! column between picker and dots,
			and MERITS/FLAWS grew 20 for theirs between name and BOOK - the widest name with its (N) cost
			needs all 264 (SPEC V349c, B171). Every box right of each moved with it; the tab closes on 1635.

			2026-09-02, T901 and T902 (SPEC I134j, I134k): MERITS and FLAWS are ONE height and FLAWS
			closes where BACKGROUNDS closes; every box right of them is ONE height with DERANGEMENTS
			the single exception; and all three right-hand columns end on that same line. Three
			closing lines for the whole tab - 345, 520, 695 - where there used to be six.

			The floor went 693 -> 695 and that is ARITHMETIC, not taste, which is why 2px show up in
			a round that changed no content: MERITS = FLAWS closing on BACKGROUNDS wants 2h+5 = floor,
			and the ten right-hand boxes on one height want 4h+15 = floor. At 693 the second gives
			169.5. At 695 they give 345 and 170, both whole. BACKGROUNDS pays for it in FOOT - its
			last row still closes at 666, so the margin goes 27 -> 29 and no row moves.

			125th round, on the user's ask: FLAWS dropped under MERITS and ALLIES / MENTOR /
			RESOURCES / GUIDES rose into the hole it left, and DERANGEMENTS did not move. Their
			HEIGHT is what changed there, 186 -> 153, and that is what makes two rows fit in the
			311 the hole gives.

			Width is the axis V298 rules: every gap between two boxes is 5, on both axes, so a box
			narrows only if the ones beside it move by exactly what it gave up. That is why the
			136th round walked all three right-hand columns left TOGETHER - the hole the two rows
			above sit in is 455 = 225 + 5 + 225 now, the way it was 485 = 240 + 5 + 240 then.

			136th round, on the user's ask (SPEC T790): the tab redistributes WIDTH into the
			merit/flaw NAME. BACKGROUNDS gave 6 - three off each side of its content, which is
			AIR and not content: the rows keep their 300 and moved 35 -> 32, because the picker
			inside cannot narrow. V312c holds every 12pt picker to the OLD 6.5 ruler and
			"Identidade Alternativa" wants 167 of its 170 - the slack R116 measured is not
			permission to spend it. The eleven boxes on
			the right gave 15 each, three columns of them. The tables took all of 6 + 3x15 = 51
			and every pixel of it went to the NAME column: 195 -> 246. The tab still closes on
			1595 and every gap is still 5: 364 + 5 + 536 + 5 + 225 + 5 + 225 + 5 + 225.

			The name is what the width was FOR. A picker CLIPS - it does not wrap - and at 195
			two of the 646 merit/flaw names did not fit in Portuguese; at 246 none of them does,
			because the longest asks 240 (SPEC V196, I107a4). The 20 the name gives back on its
			left is the column the ? button of I102b will stand in.

			The right block closes on 695 with BACKGROUNDS, which is what V289 measures - it used
			to name RESOURCES and now names OTHER, because RESOURCES went up into the hole. V290b
			was re-aimed the same way: Merit/Flaw, MENTOR/FAME and DERANGEMENTS/ARTIFACTS are the
			pairs standing over each other now.

			The 46th round put BACKGROUNDS in front of all of it and pushed the rest 330 right
			(SPEC I3, V145). The tab closes 330 further out than it did, and 160 further out
			than Main - it is the tab that reaches for a horizontal scrollbar first, which is
			the price of the box being wide enough to hold a picker and five dots.

			The outer MERITS AND FLAWS frame was removed on request (SPEC T102). The two tables
			it wrapped are unchanged in shape, just promoted to top level, and each grew from 8
			to 10 rows inside the space the frame's title and margins gave back.

			143rd round, on the user's ask: ONE more PICKED row at the TOP of each table. It is
			merit_m0 / merit_f0 and NOT a renumbering: renaming m1..m10 would drop what every
			saved sheet already holds (SPEC V2), so the new row takes the number BEFORE the
			first one and the ten keep theirs. Each table went 311 -> 336 and FLAWS fell the 25
			MERITS took, keeping the 5px gap V298 rules. T901 took the pair to 345 each and the column
			closes on 695 now, exactly where BACKGROUNDS does - the 18px of slack it used to leave under FLAWS is what the user asked to spend.
		-->
		<!--
			Two templates where there was one (SPEC I100a, T756), and the picked half carries the
			search button of I107a instead of a combo: keyboard writes NOTHING into it, only
			mfConfirm does, which makes V13's guarantee stronger here than a readOnly edit would.

			The name is dyn* on purpose (SPEC I107a3): the language traversal in WoD20.6 covers
			<button> since T14 and snapshots the AUTHORED text, so without the prefix it would
			restore `Select Merit` over the name Lua wrote, on the first language switch.

			The data does not live on the button - a button has no field. It lives in the hidden
			edt* beside it: ONE field, TWO widgets, ONE visible, which is exactly the pair the
			sheet already runs for cboClanFamily/edtClanFamily (SPEC I107a1, I71, V274).

			The picker is also the row's drag HANDLE, in both templates (SPEC I174b, V508b): the
			host's own drag-and-drop starts on it - onStartDrag hands rowDragStart the drag - and
			the whole dragRow_<field> layout around it follows, up or down only. The click stays
			the click: the host fires no onClick after a drag (SPEC R174e), so mfOpen needs no
			guard - the one it had ate the next real click (SPEC B177). The tooltip's onMouseMove
			is gated by rowDragMove: one stray move slips through right after the drag starts.

			NOTHING may be commented INSIDE a <template> - rdk exits 1 with an empty message and
			deletes the .rpk (SPEC B19).

			hit* (33rd batch, SPEC I178e, V519) is the FIRST child of both templates, behind
			everything and filling the row's layout: the tip shows anywhere on the row, gaps
			included. It is no drag handle - only the picker starts a drag (SPEC V508).
		-->
		<template name="MeritPicked">
			<rectangle name="hitmerit_$(num)" align="contents" color="#00000000" strokeColor="#00000000" hitTest="true" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, '$(sub)', 'merit_$(num)', 'hitmerit_$(num)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<button name="btnQmerit_$(num)" left="0" top="0" width="20" height="20" text="?" onClick="popOpen(self, 'Merit', sheet['merit_$(num)'], '$(sub)', 'merit_$(num)');" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, '$(sub)', 'merit_$(num)', 'btnQmerit_$(num)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<button name="dynMerit_$(num)" left="20" top="0" width="264" height="24" text="$(lbl)" onClick="mfOpen(self, 'merit_$(num)', '$(sub)', 'Merit');" onMenu="mfMenuOpen('merit_$(num)', '$(sub)');" onStartDrag="rowDragStart(self, drag, x, y, event, '$(sub)', 'merit_$(num)');" onMouseMove="if not rowDragMove(self, event) then noteTipMove(self, event, '$(sub)', 'merit_$(num)', 'dynMerit_$(num)'); end;" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<edit name="edtMerit_$(num)" left="20" top="0" width="264" height="24" field="merit_$(num)" visible="false" enabled="false"/>
			<button name="btnNmerit_$(num)" left="284" top="0" width="20" height="20" text="!" fontColor="white" onClick="noteOpen(self, '$(sub)', 'merit_$(num)');" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, '$(sub)', 'merit_$(num)', 'btnNmerit_$(num)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<edit name="edtBook_$(num)" left="304" top="0" width="234" height="24" field="book_$(num)" readOnly="true" opacity="0.75" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, '$(sub)', 'merit_$(num)', 'edtBook_$(num)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<edit name="edtType_$(num)" left="538" top="0" width="90" height="24" field="type_$(num)" readOnly="true" opacity="0.75" horzTextAlign="center" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, '$(sub)', 'merit_$(num)', 'edtType_$(num)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<edit name="edtCost_$(num)" left="628" top="0" width="75" height="24" field="costy_$(num)" readOnly="true" opacity="0.75" horzTextAlign="center" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, '$(sub)', 'merit_$(num)', 'edtCost_$(num)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
		</template>
		<!--
			PILOT of SPEC I113 (Q30, T808) - the first family to lose its dropdown for the search
			box. The row keeps its x and its five dots; what changed is the entry: a visible
			<button> named dyn* so the WoD20.6 traversal leaves the text Lua writes alone
			(I107a3), and the FIELD on a hidden <edit> beside it - one field, two widgets, one
			visible, exactly the pair MeritPicked already runs (I107a1, I71, V274).
		
			The three arguments are the whole of I113a: FIELD to write, LIST to read out of
			PICKER_LIST, and the description MODULE the pane and the ? both read.
		
			NOTHING may be commented INSIDE a <template> - rdk exits 1 with an empty message and
			deletes the .rpk (SPEC B19).
		-->
		<template name="OpenAbility">
			<rectangle name="hit$(field)" align="contents" color="#00000000" strokeColor="#00000000" hitTest="true" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'hit$(field)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<button name="btnQ$(field)" left="0" top="0" width="20" height="20" text="?" onClick="popOpen(self, 'Background', sheet['$(field)'], nil, '$(field)');" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'btnQ$(field)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<button name="dyn$(field)" left="20" top="0" width="170" height="25" text="Select Background" onClick="mfOpen(self, '$(field)', 'background', 'Background');" onMenu="mfMenuOpen('$(field)', 'background');" onStartDrag="rowDragStart(self, drag, x, y, event, 'background', '$(field)');" onMouseMove="if not rowDragMove(self, event) then noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'dyn$(field)'); end;" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<edit name="edt$(field)" left="20" top="0" width="170" height="25" field="$(field)" visible="false" enabled="false"/>
			<button name="btnN$(field)" left="190" top="0" width="20" height="20" text="!" fontColor="white" onClick="noteOpen(self, 'background', '$(field)');" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'btnN$(field)');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_1" left="215" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_1" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_1', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'dot$(field)_1');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_2" left="240" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_2" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_2', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'dot$(field)_2');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_3" left="265" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_3" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_3', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'dot$(field)_3');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_4" left="290" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_4" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_4', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'dot$(field)_4');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_5" left="315" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_5" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_5', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'dot$(field)_5');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_6" left="340" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_6" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_6', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'dot$(field)_6');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_7" left="365" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_7" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_7', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'dot$(field)_7');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_8" left="390" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_8" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_8', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'dot$(field)_8');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_9" left="415" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_9" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_9', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'dot$(field)_9');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="dot$(field)_10" left="440" top="0" width="25" height="25" field="$(field)_10" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" autoChange="false" onClick="xpClick('$(field)_10', self);" onMouseMove="noteTipMove(self, event, 'background', '$(field)', 'dot$(field)_10');" onMouseLeave="noteTipLeave(self);" visible="false"/>
		</template>

		<!--
			The last five rows are TYPED, not picked (SPEC I50, V255, user 2026-08-22): the same
			shape the Ghoul tab got in the 85th round and SPECIALTIES got beside it - same entry x,
			same five dots at the same prices, `edt` instead of `cbo` so pickerItems and PICKER_LIST
			never reach them (SPEC V211a, V26).

			A typed background is still a background: it keeps xpClick on every dot, so what the
			storyteller writes is bought and priced exactly like what the book offers (SPEC I9).

			No comment lives INSIDE the template - one there makes rdk -l exit 1 with no message and
			delete the .rpk (SPEC B19, the fifth door, 85th round).
		-->

		<!-- The storyteller's backgrounds moved here from the Main tab in the 46th round
		     (SPEC I3, V145): to the LEFT of the merit table, bottom flush with FLAWS and OTHER
		     (y=679 since SPEC I186, V289, V392c). The height bought eleven more rows - twenty at the same 30px pitch, the
		     twenty-first would need 650 and there is only 640. Every other box on the tab
		     moved 330 right: 320 wide plus the 10px gutter the tab already keeps.

		     320 is the width the box had on Main and cannot shrink: the row inside is 290 -
		     a 160px picker and five 25px dots.

		     The row count lives in BACKGROUND_ROWS on the root form (SPEC V145). A row added
		     here and nowhere else would be a background nothing prices: free, and invisible
		     in the log.

		     Every row layout here, in MERITS and in FLAWS is named dragRow_<field> (SPEC I174a):
		     a drag moves it by top and never moves its data, and the top written here is the
		     factory order - what a sheet with no orderBackground/orderMerit/orderFlaw shows.
		     One pitch per box (30 here, 25 in the other two), the one ROW_LISTS reads. -->
		<layout name="boxBackgrounds" left="0" top="0" width="384" height="679">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="20" top="15" width="344" height="20" text="BACKGROUNDS" horzTextAlign="center" anchors="left top right"/>

			<layout name="dragRow_background_1" left="20" top="36" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_1"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_2" left="20" top="66" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_2"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_3" left="20" top="96" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_3"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_4" left="20" top="126" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_4"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_5" left="20" top="156" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_5"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_6" left="20" top="186" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_6"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_7" left="20" top="216" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_7"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_8" left="20" top="246" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_8"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_9" left="20" top="276" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_9"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_10" left="20" top="306" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_10"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_11" left="20" top="336" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_11"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_12" left="20" top="366" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_12"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_13" left="20" top="396" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_13"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_14" left="20" top="426" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_14"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_15" left="20" top="456" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_15"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_16" left="20" top="486" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_16"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_17" left="20" top="516" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_17"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_18" left="20" top="546" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_18"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_19" left="20" top="576" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_19"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_20" left="20" top="606" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_20"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_background_21" left="20" top="636" width="340" height="25" anchors="left top right" >
				<OpenAbility field="background_21"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<layout name="boxMerits" left="389" top="0" width="743" height="337">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="40" top="15" width="264" height="20" text="MERITS" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<label left="324" top="15" width="234" height="20" text="BOOK" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<!-- Column renamed to Page on request. The field is still type_* : renaming a
			     field drops what is already saved in existing sheets (SPEC V2). -->
			<label left="558" top="15" width="90" height="20" text="PAGE" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<label left="648" top="15" width="75" height="20" text="COST" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<layout name="dragRow_merit_m0" left="20" top="36" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="merit" num="m0" lbl="Select Merit"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_m1" left="20" top="61" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="merit" num="m1" lbl="Select Merit"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_m2" left="20" top="86" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="merit" num="m2" lbl="Select Merit"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_m3" left="20" top="111" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="merit" num="m3" lbl="Select Merit"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_m4" left="20" top="136" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="merit" num="m4" lbl="Select Merit"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_m5" left="20" top="161" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="merit" num="m5" lbl="Select Merit"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_m6" left="20" top="186" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="merit" num="m6" lbl="Select Merit"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_m7" left="20" top="211" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="merit" num="m7" lbl="Select Merit"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_m8" left="20" top="236" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="merit" num="m8" lbl="Select Merit"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_m9" left="20" top="261" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="merit" num="m9" lbl="Select Merit"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_m10" left="20" top="286" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="merit" num="m10" lbl="Select Merit"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<layout name="boxFlaws" left="389" top="342" width="743" height="337">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="40" top="15" width="264" height="20" text="FLAWS" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<label left="324" top="15" width="234" height="20" text="BOOK" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<label left="558" top="15" width="90" height="20" text="PAGE" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<label left="648" top="15" width="75" height="20" text="COST" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<layout name="dragRow_merit_f0" left="20" top="36" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="flaw" num="f0" lbl="Select Flaw"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_f1" left="20" top="61" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="flaw" num="f1" lbl="Select Flaw"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_f2" left="20" top="86" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="flaw" num="f2" lbl="Select Flaw"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_f3" left="20" top="111" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="flaw" num="f3" lbl="Select Flaw"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_f4" left="20" top="136" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="flaw" num="f4" lbl="Select Flaw"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_f5" left="20" top="161" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="flaw" num="f5" lbl="Select Flaw"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_f6" left="20" top="186" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="flaw" num="f6" lbl="Select Flaw"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_f7" left="20" top="211" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="flaw" num="f7" lbl="Select Flaw"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_f8" left="20" top="236" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="flaw" num="f8" lbl="Select Flaw"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_f9" left="20" top="261" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="flaw" num="f9" lbl="Select Flaw"/>
			</layout>
			<layout name="dragRow_merit_f10" left="20" top="286" width="703" height="25" >
				<MeritPicked sub="flaw" num="f10" lbl="Select Flaw"/>
			</layout>
		</layout>

		<!-- 42nd batch (SPEC I186b/c): the nine note boxes beside these two left on request and their
		     fields are declared ORPHANS (SPEC I3) - a saved sheet keeps the text, nothing shows it.
		     DERANGEMENTS and OTHER are the twins of MERITS and FLAWS on the Y axis now (SPEC V392b),
		     5px right of them. -->
		<layout name="boxDerangements" left="1137" top="0" width="225" height="337">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="20" top="15" width="185" height="20" text="DERANGEMENTS" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<textEditor left="35" top="36" width="155" height="284" field="derangements"/>
		</layout>

		<layout name="boxOther" left="1137" top="342" width="225" height="337">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label left="20" top="15" width="185" height="20" text="OTHER" horzTextAlign="center"/>

			<!-- ponytail: the plain "other" field name is already owned by WoD20.3.lfm sheet-wide; renamed to bgOther per SPEC V1 -->
			<textEditor left="35" top="36" width="155" height="284" field="bgOther"/>
		</layout>


		<!--
			SPEC I170h, T1077 - the ! note's tooltip. LAST child of the scrollBox, so it paints over
			every box and scrolls with them: its left/top are CONTENT coordinates, the same space the
			box layouts' own left/top live in, and noteTipMove reaches them in two parent hops from
			the control under the pointer (control -> row layout -> box). The era's box colour at 80% -
			authored black, which applyTheme maps to the fill of every box, plus opacity - with NO
			outline and NO title, the text alone (SPEC V501a, I177a, I178c); no xradius, so it is no box; contents, not client, for the background, so it does not compete
			with the scrollBox for the client rect (SPEC V190). Since the 66th batch (user 2026-10-03,
			SPEC I209) it has NO scrollBox: the label sits straight in the tip, 5 from each edge, and
			a long note is broken and cut by tipLayout (at most 480 x 270, "...") instead of scrolling. Entering holds
			the tip open while leaving hides it (SPEC V501b/d).
		-->
		<layout name="noteTip" left="0" top="0" width="300" height="60" visible="false" onMouseEnter="noteTipHold(self);" onMouseLeave="noteTipHide(self);">
			<rectangle align="contents" color="black" opacity="0.80" strokeColor="#00000000" hitTest="false"/>
			<label name="dynNoteTip" left="5" top="5" width="276" height="20" fontSize="12" wordWrap="false" autoSize="true" textTrimming="none" onResize="noteTipFit(self, 'noteTip', 'dynNoteTip');"/>
		</layout>
	</scrollBox>
</form>
